    "description": "Hemingray Glass Insulators - 3 Piece Lot\nHemingray No. 12, CD 113\nAqua Blue-Green, Vintage Mid-Century\nThis lot features three vintage glass telegraph/telephone insulators produced by the Hemingray Glass Company, once the world's largest manufacturer of glass insulators. The No. 12 model was a standard utility piece used extensively across North American communication lines. Today, these pieces are highly sought after by collectors for their historical significance, industrial aesthetic, and the iconic aqua color characteristic of Hemingray production.\nPieces Included:\nGlass Insulator, Hemingray No. 12, Aqua, Drip Point Base - Visible base chip\nGlass Insulator, Hemingray No. 12, Aqua, Drip Point Base - Minor base roughness\nGlass Insulator, Hemingray No. 12, Aqua, Drip Point Base - Small skirt chips\nCondition:\nThese pieces show varying degrees of wear consistent with salvaged utility glass. One insulator has a significant chip/chunk missing from the bottom skirt edge as shown in photos. The remaining two pieces show smaller fleabites, surface scratches, and general rim roughness along the base edges. The molded \"HEMINGRAY No 12\" marks remain legible on all pieces, and the glass retains its original color and clarity with typical manufacturing bubbles and mold lines.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
